WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.200
- Hi, I'm after yours.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.058
- Oh my god, I'm after yours!

00:00:03.058 --> 00:00:06.360
We should tradesies after the show.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.193
Well, I'm gonna start with-

00:00:07.193 --> 00:00:08.760
wait, congratulations, new son, right?

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.840
- Yes, thank you very much.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:10.673
Yeah, six months old.

00:00:10.673 --> 00:00:11.506
- [Kelly] Six months.

00:00:11.506 --> 00:00:13.140
Oh, are you sleeping?

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.370
- Yeah, he's doing okay.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.035
He's sleeping more than we are.

00:00:16.035 --> 00:00:17.430
(all laugh)

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.280
- So you have a two-year-old, right?

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.120
Do you do Halloween?

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.200
Do y'all get all done up?

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.033
I love Halloween.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:25.680
- As someone who dresses up for a living,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.540
it's not my favorite
thing to put on a costume,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.700
but of course, my
daughter really wanted us

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:30.783
to do Frozen.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.270
So she's Anna and I am gonna be Elsa,

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.678
and my partner's gonna be Kristoff

00:00:38.678 --> 00:00:40.770
and so that's fun.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.290
She has no idea that Uncle
Jonathan is Kristoff yet.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.860
That'll be mind-blowing when
she figures that out, but.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:47.777
- Oh my god, yeah, she would lose it.

00:00:47.777 --> 00:00:49.440
But it is funny when-

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.510
'cause my kids saw an
animated thing that I did

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.670
and they were like, it broke the wall

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.469
and it was kind of intensely sad.

00:00:56.469 --> 00:00:57.420
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.830
They saw me in this movie
called "Ugly Dolls,"

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.360
and they were like, "we don't understand,"

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.770
and I was like, "well,
you know, like Elsa,

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.090
you know, she's a real person."

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.170
and they were like, "what?"

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.190
And I was like, "oh my god."

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.353
- Oh no.

00:01:06.353 --> 00:01:07.186
What have I ruined?

00:01:07.186 --> 00:01:08.688
- I felt like a horrible human,

00:01:08.688 --> 00:01:11.400
but, you know, it was gonna
happen sooner or later.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.467
- I do that to kids on
a regular basis when-

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:15.300
like, "It's Harry!"

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.290
I'm like, "I'm sorry."

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:17.190
They're like, "you're old now!

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.023
What happened?"

00:01:18.023 --> 00:01:20.430
(all laugh)

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.390
- So that was what's so funny.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.520
My daughter was obsessed
with Chris Martin for like-

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.080
I mean, years, and she always watched

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.880
the "Yellow" video, but he's younger.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.800
It's his first single, and
so whenever she saw him,

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.030
she's like, "well, he looks different."

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.430
I go, "well, we age, honey."

